															</div>
				<div class="info">
					<span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/misterbibs" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(453823); return false;"  ><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=453823&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1609579086" alt="MisterBibs" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=453823)"/></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/misterbibs" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(453823); return false;" >MisterBibs</a></span> <span class="odate time_1335838764 format_%25e%20%25b%20%25Y%2C%20%25H%3A%25M%7Cagohover">01 May 2012 02:19</span>
														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-1433695">
									

<p>I've got a bit more interestingly random facts about this story, now that I'm done at work and can talk a bit more.</p>
<p>There's no real references to anything in the story. Actually, that's a bit of a lie: there's references to stories that I had considered writing, or tried to write but decided to abandon. First and foremost is a character trait for Character-Bibs that I'm still considering exploring: Character-Bibs has to be forced to take vacations in a meaningful away. I really like the concept of Clef stealing Bib's access card (so he can't just work during his vacation) and that Bibs has a tertiary work tablet because he expects his primary and secondary ones to be taken away from him during his off-times. In my headcannon, the Foundation is vaguely aware that Bibs goes rogue during these vacations. He does what he <em>wants</em> to do, the way he <em>wants</em> to do it, and can claim that he wasn't doing any official work. It's a concept I want to explore, but the time I tried it, it wound up being too Mary Sueish.</p>

							</div>

								
					
